<p>This route does the following:</p>
<ol>
<li>It responds to GET requests to the <code>/users</code> URL.</li>
<li>It uses a closure function to define the route&#x27;s behavior.</li>
<li>Inside the closure, it fetches all users from the database using the <code>User</code> model.</li>
<li>It returns a view named <code>users.index</code>, passing the fetched users to the view.</li>
</ol>
<p>While this approach works for simple routes, it&#x27;s generally not recommended for larger applications. As your application grows, putting logic directly in route closures can lead to cluttered and hard-to-maintain code.</p>
